course: dictionary
lesson: 2249
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and «crane» is a good example. The clues around the word tell you which meaning is right. Ask yourself: what is happening here, and which meaning would fit?
explain: «The crane lifted the heavy steel beams onto the roof.» Lifting heavy beams and a roof tell you a crane is a machine. «The crane stood on one leg by the lake.» A lake and standing on one leg tell you a crane is a bird.
explain: «Mia craned her neck to see over the crowd.» Here crane is a action word. It means stretching your neck to see better. Check your meaning by swapping it in: "Mia stretched her neck to see over the crowd" still makes sense.
fact: A crane can be a very tall machine with a long arm that lifts heavy things, such as a tower crane on a building site.
fact: A crane can also be a large bird with long legs, a long neck and a long beak.
fact: To crane your neck is to stretch your neck to see something better.
fact: The red-crowned crane stands about 1.5 metres tall, and in China and Japan it is a symbol of good luck and long life.
fact: Crane is a noun (a crane, cranes) and a verb (craned, craning), so check which job the word does in the sentence.
exercise: «The crane lifted the heavy steel beams onto the roof.» What is a crane in this sentence? | To stretch your neck to see better | A paper toy folded for a wish | *A tall machine with a long arm | A large bird with long legs
exercise: «Look up in winter and you may see cranes flying with their necks stretched out.» What kind of crane is this? | A tall tower with a long arm | A way of stretching your neck | *A large bird | A machine on a building site
exercise: «Mia craned her neck to see over the crowd.» What does craned mean? | Flew away quickly | Folded a paper bird | *Stretched her neck to see better | Lifted heavy things with a machine
test: «A mobile crane is a crane on a lorry with an arm that slides out like a telescope.» What is a mobile crane? | A way of stretching your neck | A bird that lives near water | *A crane on a lorry with a sliding arm | A paper bird folded for a wish
test: «The red-crowned crane is a symbol of good luck and long life.» What does symbol mean here? | A sound that a bird makes | *Something that stands for an idea, such as good luck | A kind of machine on a building site | A map of where the bird lives
exam: «A crane can lift a car, while a crane in the marsh can stand very still.» Which two meanings of crane are used? | A bird and a verb | Two ways to stretch your neck | Two birds | *A machine and a bird
